      "findings": [
        {
          "severity": "p1",
          "where": "ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py:238-251,292-297,345-356 \u2194 coordination.py@7a1a7320:265,515-1250",
          "claim": "The delivered coordination core exposes `resolve(conn)` and CLI-oriented `do_*` verbs, while this server invokes `resolve()` without a connection and searches only for bare `verb`/`verb_` functions. Composition raises an uncaught TypeError before authorization; `coord_resolve` also collides with the participant resolver. Consequently valid tools/call and resources/read requests can terminate without a JSON-RPC result or refusal-wire line.",
          "reproduce": "nl -ba ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py | sed -n '238,297p'; git -C /home/scientdb/projects/uscient/agentscient show 7a1a7320:ops/conductor/tools/coordination.py | rg -n '^def (resolve|do_(brief|submit|resolve|observe))\\('"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p2",
          "where": "ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py:142-147; ops/conductor/coordination-mcp-lever.md:222-227 \u2194 coordination.py@7a1a7320:938-956",
          "claim": "`coord_observe` is an assignment write but omits `generation`; the delivered core also inserts an observation as `current` without checking generation or matching its revision to the assignment. A stale participant can therefore append an old-revision observation after `reopen`, defeating the stated stale-generation and observation-freshness guarantees.",
          "reproduce": "sed -n '142,147p' ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py; git -C /home/scientdb/projects/uscient/agentscient show 7a1a7320:ops/conductor/tools/coordination.py | sed -n '938,958p'"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p2",
          "where": "ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py:87-90,133-140,345-356,458-486",
          "claim": "None of the contract's three runtime bounds is implemented: list tools have no cursor, core calls are direct and have no timeout, and responses pass straight to stdout without a size cap or overflow reading. A slow core blocks the single request loop, while a large assignment/message result produces an unbounded response.",
          "reproduce": "PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'ops/conductor/tools'); import coordination_mcp as m; m._send({'x':'x'*70000})\" | wc -c"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p2",
          "where": "ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py:409-449",
          "claim": "Method-specific parameter validation is absent for initialize, ping, tools/list, and resources/list. For example, an unknown ping parameter and a non-string initialize protocolVersion both return successful results instead of the contract's -32602 Invalid params response.",
          "reproduce": "printf '%s\\n' '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"ping\",\"params\":{\"bogus\":1}}' '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":[]}}' | PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -B ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py serve"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p2",
          "where": "ops/conductor/registry/coordination_mcp.py.json:1; ops/conductor/coordination-mcp-lever.md:295-298",
          "claim": "The contract requires conformance invocations for both `config` and `identity`, but the registry contains `config` and `arguments`, both marked `identity:false`. The conventions suite therefore does not classify this mutation server as a writing instrument and cannot detect a missing or malformed identity refusal.",
          "reproduce": "sed -n '1p' ops/conductor/registry/coordination_mcp.py.json"
        },
        {
          "severity": "p3",
          "where": "ops/conductor/tools/coordination_mcp.py:256-269,302-356",
          "claim": "Capability-first validation can return a misleading privilege-expansion remedy for a request that is independently malformed: an empty allowlist plus missing coord_observe arguments says to obtain that capability, and only after it is granted reports the missing arguments. Caller-supplied authority keys are exceptionally validated before capability, so the ordering is also non-uniform and does not provide the claimed argument-shape concealment.",
          "reproduce": null
        }
